{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1127","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1127","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1127\",\"parent_revision\":\"8eb27179621d4a314ac7daa3358a5b033f73df5a\",\"root_revision\":\"c1360ac776a9989fde025e75d94dfa3a978638a0b43d5ca281251c15390fe5de\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n20+ test files directly call underscore-prefixed private functions, creating coupling that prevents safe refactoring. Audit identified three categories:\\n\\n**Unjustifiable (has public path \u2014 migrate to public API):**\\n- `test_registry_loader.py`: `RegistryLoader._apply_extension` \u2014 testable via `merge_type`\\n- `test_addressing.py`: `_reject_path_traversal` \u2014 testable via `parse_address`\\n- `test_batch_section_writes.py`: `ops._handle_batch_groomed` \u2014 testable via `groom_item`\\n- `test_ac_overlap_warning.py`: `ops._check_ac_overlap` \u2014 testable via `update_item`\\n- `test_paginate_body.py`: `ops._paginate_body` \u2014 testable via `view_item`\\n\\n**Justified but undocumented (add inline comment):**\\n- `test_reader_bugfixes.py`: regression tests for confirmed data-loss bugs\\n- `test_cli_migrate_fallback.py`: `_migrate_one` / `_migrate_one_fallback` \u2014 no coarser public path\\n\\n**Algorithmic helpers (document deliberate contract):**\\n- `_keys_to_kebab`, `_resolve_labels_graphql`, `_build_artifact_content_comment`, `_extract_content_from_comment`, `_dedup_by_name_priority`\\n\\nAction: migrate unjustifiable cases to public API, add `# white-box test: <reason>` comments to justified cases, create `TESTING.md` convention doc.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-29T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-29T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **document and triage private method testing across the test suite** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Test quality audit 2026-03-29\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n5/10 \u2014 Reduces coupling that blocks safe refactoring. Not urgent (no active refactoring blocked today), but accumulates technical debt as the test suite grows.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Safe renaming and extraction of private helpers (tests break on internal renames even when public behavior is unchanged)\\n- Bottleneck: CI noise and false-negative test failures during refactors; reviewers cannot tell which private-method tests are intentional vs accidental\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Migrating unjustifiable tests to public-API paths makes them resilient to internal restructuring\\n- Inline `# white-box test:` comments make intentional coupling self-documenting\\n- TESTING.md convention doc prevents new unjustifiable tests from being added silently\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nAll tests in the suite fall into exactly one documented category:\\n1. Public-API tests \u2014 exercise observable behavior only (no underscore imports)\\n2. White-box tests \u2014 import private symbols, annotated with `# white-box test: <reason>` explaining why no public path exists\\n3. Algorithmic-helper tests \u2014 isolated pure-function tests, annotated with `# white-box test: pure algorithmic helper \u2014 no public path`\\n\\nA TESTING.md file at the plugin root defines these categories and gives examples of each.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -r 'from.*import.*_[a-z]\\\\|import.*\\\\._[a-z]' plugins/development-harness/tests plugins/development-harness/tests_sam plugins/scientific-method/mcp/experiment-registry/tests` returns only lines that have a `# white-box test:` comment on the same line or the preceding line\\n2. The five unjustifiable private-method test files no longer import the private symbol directly \u2014 they exercise the same behavior via the documented public path\\n3. `grep -r 'white-box test' plugins/development-harness/tests plugins/development-harness/tests_sam` returns at least one match per justified file (`test_reader_bugfixes.py`, `test_cli_migrate_fallback.py`, algorithmic helpers)\\n4. A `TESTING.md` file exists at `plugins/development-harness/TESTING.md` (or repo root) defining the three categories with examples\\n5. All existing tests still pass: `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests plugins/development-harness/tests_sam -q` exits 0\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Test file | plugins/scientific-method/mcp/experiment-registry/tests/test_registry_loader.py |\\n| Test file | plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_addressing.py |\\n| Test file | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_batch_section_writes.py |\\n| Test file | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_ac_overlap_warning.py |\\n| Test file | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_paginate_body.py |\\n| Test file | plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_reader_bugfixes.py |\\n| Test file | plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_cli_migrate_fallback.py |\\n| Test file | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_yaml_writer.py |\\n| Test file | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_manifest_discovery.py |\\n| Test file | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_artifact_content_storage.py |\\n| Source file | plugins/scientific-method/mcp/experiment-registry/registry_loader.py (`merge_type` public path for `_apply_extension`) |\\n| Source file | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py (`_resolve_labels_graphql`) |\\n| Source file | plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py (`_keys_to_kebab`) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: Any refactor that renames or extracts a private helper tested by the unjustifiable files\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 5 migration targets require reading the public API path, writing replacement tests, and verifying they cover the same cases. 2 justified files need annotation only. 3 algorithmic-helper files need annotation only. TESTING.md is a new ~1-page document. Estimated 2\u20134 hours of focused work across the three categories.\\n\",\"digest\":\"2a9b5c8fc2a9542fbc496cd1e7a437155bb477a03ae7f64b26075bc085709adf\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg6G2A\"}"}